# WB17: the lane B opening rule (D41 / LB4; TB17, TB18).
# The driver's tick decides the gate by [lane_b] open_rule:
#   "cogate"            today's gate_open (routing co-gate), unchanged;
#   "tokens"            lineage_tokens >= open_tokens (D41 b);
#   "tokens_king_check" lineage_tokens >= open_tokens AND the latest lane A
#                       king check (ops.king_check()) has result "pass" (D41 a).
# While closed it records a typed gate_closed_reason; when it opens it records
# gate_rule (the configured rule) and gate_evidence (the satisfying facts,
# strict JSON) in LaneBDriverState, a one-way latch that survives restart.
# RunnerLaneBOps gains king_check() over the runner's verified receipt read.
